+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01DBXwmhtPuxLCMSMVenR73q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is clean: lint passes, build passes, 34 tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI built a reactive spreadsheet engine as a TypeScript library, organized into focused modules under `src/`:\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| `references.ts` | Cell-ref parsing, bijective base-26 column ↔ index conversion, range expansion |\n| `tokenizer.ts` | Lexer for formula expressions (numbers, strings, identifiers, operators) |\n| `ast.ts` | AST node type definitions |\n| `parser.ts` | Recursive-descent parser with correct operator precedence |\n| `evaluator.ts` | Evaluates an AST against a cell resolver; functions, comparisons, errors |\n| `values.ts` | Value types, error representation, display formatting |\n| `spreadsheet.ts` | The `Spreadsheet` class: dependency graph, cycle detection, reactive recompute |\n| `index.ts` | Public exports |\n\n**Key design points:**\n\n- **Reactive updates** — each cell tracks `dependencies` and `dependents`. On `set()`, only the changed cell and its transitive dependents are recomputed, in topological order (Kahn's algorithm restricted to the affected subgraph) so every cell sees fresh inputs and each is computed once.\n- **Cycle detection** — before mutating any state, a DFS over the dependency graph (substituting the new dependency set) checks whether the assignment would reach back to the cell. If so it throws and leaves state untouched (verified by a test).\n- **Empty-cell handling** — referencing an empty cell still creates a dependency edge, so dependents update when that cell is later populated; empty cells aren't reported by `getCells()`.\n- **Functions** — `SUM`/`AVERAGE`/`MIN`/`MAX`/`COUNT` operate over expanded ranges ignoring non-numeric cells; `IF` with full comparison operator support; nesting works.\n- **Errors** — division by zero, value errors, etc. propagate as spreadsheet-style codes (`#DIV/0!`, `#VALUE!`) rather than throwing; only malformed formulas and circular refs throw at `set()` time.\n\nThe example usage from the spec all produces the expected results, and the full suite of 34 Vitest tests covers values, arithmetic, precedence, reactivity (chains, diamonds, dependency replacement), all functions, comparisons, circular references, multi-letter columns, and error propagation."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":276,"cache_read_input_tokens":51148,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":276},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c2a4297-d5f5-4e02-8bfc-d3d790dc970f","uuid":"b9d5d48b-4dbc-4e99-b3c1-568ac8ba3fd4","request_id":"req_011CbVdBS4hHeQ3FX3xGFRZ8"}
